#{[17592186289558 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, III, and IV" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289558 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289558 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e6200ebf-b364-55da-8734-0d50031c5a08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186289338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289840 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3459c60d-978a-5a3f-861a-110bccb1e94a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186289213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289984 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "74ce7f3d-ede3-5d56-84d2-9fd025fc8f92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290329 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290329 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216042" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290329 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290329 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3p+\\frac{4}{5}q=-1 \\\\ 9p-4q=-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290329 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "906fc64a-e7c8-5770-89dc-d9c9f6b082d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290329 #edb/ref 1074 "To get rid of the fractions in the first equation, we must multiply the first equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $5.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3p+\\frac{4}{5}q=-1 & |\\,\\times 5 \\\\ 9p-4q=-13\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-15p+4q=-5 \\\\ 9p-4q=-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that the $4q$ term in the first equation can cancel with the $-4q$ term in the second equation.\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $q$-variable, and allows us to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15p+\\cancel{4q} & =-5 \\\\ 9p-\\cancel{4q} & =-13 \\\\ -6p & =-18 \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $p=3$ into the equation $9p-4q=-13$ to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9p-4q & =-13 \\\\ 9\\cdot 3-4q & =-13 \\\\ 27-4q & =-13 \\\\ -4q & =-40 \\\\ q & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=3,\\,q=10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290566 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290566 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2469" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290566 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290566 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)<0$\n- $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(1)>0$\n- $x=1$ is a relative maximum of $f(x)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290566 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "54523433-2b3d-5350-9453-344ec229fc6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290566 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12x-12{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-12{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12x(1-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12-24x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =12>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-12<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false while statement VI is true. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290656 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290656 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290656 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "043c68c8-e391-5780-a3ff-6d80dc52b081" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291191 #edb/ref 1080 "x=4,\\,y=4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291191 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291191 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83f90f5e-a59d-5dbb-b7bc-2235614d11e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291213 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-4,\\,y=6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291213 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291213 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88278ddc-f2aa-572e-bfa1-75529cee7a88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291224 #edb/ref 1080 "x=2,\\,y=2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291224 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291224 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8b6b2395-ed33-5ae6-ab41-6b9f005b95ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291265 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417]