 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186300522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186301203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186300447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301729 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9bc72922-bebc-50a1-a8ff-483d8fbfcfc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & 4x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "534e2a93-e71a-5475-894e-dfd5ca99a3a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302109 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & k+2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & (k+2)y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nNow if $k=-2$, then the second equation is $0=-2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when  $k=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302361 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302361 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32785" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302361 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302361 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3t-3 \\\\ y=7-9t \\\\ z=\\frac{3}{2}t-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302361 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9af4fe7c-30e2-5561-acae-f8071602310e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302361 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3t-3 \\\\ 7-9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-3,7,-\\frac{1}{2})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302540 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302540 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302540 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0cc17225-6297-5308-8f48-05ff9ca8b564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302834 #edb/re